A||N||3||Freshj||Porting Exhaust Manifolds on V6||||1||
Z||000000||Freshj||11-15-2001||11:17 PM||||Ok, from what I hear you tend to get better performance from porting the stock manifolds over the Sprint headers (especially for the price diff). Is there anyway of getting them off w/o dropping the cradle? I know the front won't be hard but what about the back?||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||11-16-2001||02:37 AM||||you can drop just the rear of the cradle and make it much easier........ here is what I would do...... jack up the car and place two small jack stands just forward of the front cradle mounts, take off the rear wheels, place the jack under the rear cross-member, remove one end of the upper engine strut (dogbone), remove the two rear cradle bolts, lower the jack and the cradle will swing down making it much easier to remove the manifold -- I would also spray the manifold bolts with penetrating oil before removing them. Once one breaks then it is easy-out time and a real pain to do........ By the way, if you haven't changed plugs on a tune-up recently, now is the time to do it!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||WampusCat||11-16-2001||05:45 AM||||Are the welds going to be OK after grinding material from the inside of the tubes?  Do you need to add some weld to the outside of the joints?||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||11-16-2001||02:54 PM||||As far as I know, yes, the welds should be 'beefed up'.  As the pipes are stainless steel, your welder must use stainless rod as well.  Supposedly good for 8 - 10 HP.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
